Description: Use system Korean font instead of Nanum
 This patch removes CSS references to Nanum. As refrenced by
 LP: #2031685, we already have Korean glyph coverage in the default
 system fonts, so we want to avoid pulling fonts-nanum into main.
Author: Zixing Liu <zixing.liu@canonical.com>
Bug-Ubuntu: https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/rustc/+bug/2031685
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-01-07
